<section class="section faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div><p class="section-kicker">Before you make an edition</p><h2 class="shead" id="faq-title">Questions<br />writers ask.</h2></div><details open><summary>What does it cost?</summary><p>Creating your edition and receiving the complete PDF are free. Readers pay Lulu per copy, plus shipping, applicable fees and tax. The published 294-page caithrin edition was listed at its $9.34 print cost; one real order totalled $16.58. Your preview estimates your edition from its page count. Final checkout prices come from Lulu.</p></details><details><summary>How do my subscribers buy it?</summary><p>Once you approve the proof and the edition is listed, add a custom button to a Substack post. Label it “Get a print copy” and link directly to the edition's Lulu page. Lulu takes payment, prints the copy and ships it. We help you add the finished purchase link to your Substack.</p></details><details><summary>Can I earn from each copy?</summary><p>To sell to subscribers, use your own Lulu account and choose your markup. During the beta, we guide you through setting up the listing. For personal copies, Inksheaf can host it.</p></details><details><summary>Can I print any Substack?</summary><p>This beta is for publication owners printing their own work. You retain ownership. We confirm your permission and you approve the proof before an edition is listed.</p></details><details><summary>Can I choose the design?</summary><p>Yes. Choose from four covers, using your publication's name and original logo. Read an actual excerpt and inspect print pages in the preview. You review the full proof before anything prints.</p></details><details><summary>What is the book like?</summary><p>A 6 × 9 inch matte paperback, perfect bound. We recommend volumes below 300 pages. A longer archive can become a set of quarterly volumes. The current production system refuses volumes above 800 pages.</p></details><details><summary>What about paid posts?</summary><p>The public preview reads public posts. To include paid writing, send your own Substack export during onboarding; we do not need your password. Subscriber files are deleted unread; the posts are kept for your edition.</p></details><details><summary>What happens to images and embeds?</summary><p>Images are included where available. Missing images are flagged; video, tweets and other web-only embeds receive printed source notes. We review these with you in the proof.</p></details><details><summary>Where do you ship, and when?</summary><p>Lulu’s available destinations, shipping options and prices are confirmed before ordering. Creators selling internationally are responsible for their seller and tax obligations. Making a PDF does not order a book.</p></details><details><summary>Is there an edition already?</summary><p>Yes: the caithrin collected essays, 40 pieces from January 2025 to August 2026, 294 pages. <a href="https://www.lulu.com/shop/caithrin-rintoul/caithrin-collected-essays-20252026/paperback/product-m2v2e82.html">See the existing edition on Lulu.</a> The spread above comes from its print file.</p></details><details><summary>Who can I talk to?</summary><p>Caithrin, at <a href="mailto:caithrin@caithrin.com">caithrin@caithrin.com</a>. Feedback goes directly to the builder.</p></details></section>
